WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.966
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online IELTS preparation.

2
00:00:06.266 --> 00:00:09.919
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.219 --> 00:00:17.864
Unit nine: Reading: Sentence and Summary Completion. Today you will complete sentences and summaries with words from the text.

4
00:00:18.164 --> 00:00:20.851
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.091
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:26.661
Gap.

7
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.731
Gap means an empty space to fill.

8
00:00:30.317 --> 00:00:31.562
Fill in each gap.

9
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:34.500
Your turn. Say: Gap.

10
00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:37.973
Gap.

11
00:00:38.717 --> 00:00:39.787
Word bank.

12
00:00:40.783 --> 00:00:43.526
Word bank means a list of words to choose from.

13
00:00:44.117 --> 00:00:45.710
Choose from the word bank.

14
00:00:46.317 --> 00:00:48.830
Your turn. Say: Word bank.

15
00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:52.772
Word bank.

16
00:00:53.517 --> 00:00:54.634
Grammar fit.

17
00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:59.612
Grammar fit means the word form that fits the sentence.

18
00:01:00.217 --> 00:01:02.309
Check the grammar fit of the answer.

19
00:01:02.917 --> 00:01:05.697
Your turn. Say: Grammar fit.

20
00:01:08.533 --> 00:01:09.790
Grammar fit.

21
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:11.748
Noun phrase.

22
00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.980
Noun phrase means a noun with its describing words.

23
00:01:16.583 --> 00:01:18.513
The gap needs a noun phrase.

24
00:01:19.117 --> 00:01:22.512
Your turn. Say: Noun phrase.

25
00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:26.809
Noun phrase.

26
00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:28.493
Verb form.

27
00:01:29.483 --> 00:01:31.866
Verb form means the tense or shape of a verb.

28
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.252
Check the verb form.

29
00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:37.584
Your turn. Say: Verb form.

30
00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.492
Verb form.

31
00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:43.112
Synonym.

32
00:01:44.117 --> 00:01:47.173
Synonym means a word with a similar meaning.

33
00:01:47.783 --> 00:01:49.400
The text uses a synonym.

34
00:01:49.983 --> 00:01:52.845
Your turn. Say: Synonym.

35
00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:56.736
Synonym.

36
00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:58.461
Exact.

37
00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:01.577
Exact means completely correct.

38
00:02:02.183 --> 00:02:04.589
Copy the exact word from the text.

39
00:02:05.183 --> 00:02:07.778
Your turn. Say: Exact.

40
00:02:10.633 --> 00:02:11.600
Exact.

41
00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:13.560
Instruction.

42
00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:17.072
Instruction means a rule for how to answer.

43
00:02:17.683 --> 00:02:19.358
Read the instruction first.

44
00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.486
Your turn. Say: Instruction.

45
00:02:25.333 --> 00:02:26.474
Instruction.

46
00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:30.778
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:34.708
Visal, what is the first step in summary completion?

48
00:02:35.817 --> 00:02:45.574
Read the instruction and the word limit. Then read the summary to understand the topic and decide what type of word fits each gap.

49
00:02:46.683 --> 00:02:48.207
Where do the answers come from?

50
00:02:49.317 --> 00:02:58.854
You use words from the passage, exactly as they appear. If the word limit is one word, do not write two, and do not change the spelling.

51
00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.613
How do I check my answer?

52
00:03:02.717 --> 00:03:13.345
Read the sentence again with your answer in the gap. It must be grammatical and must match the meaning of the text, with a synonym in the summary for the passage word.

53
00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.302
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:21.959
Grammar focus: Strategy: check meaning, grammar and word limit.

55
00:03:22.259 --> 00:03:23.492
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:24.183 --> 00:03:27.530
The gap needs a noun, so choose a noun phrase from the text.

57
00:03:28.417 --> 00:03:31.090
Copy the exact word and check the word limit.

58
00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:40.758
Predict the word type for each gap, find the matching idea in the text, and copy exactly. Read the finished sentence to check meaning and grammar.

59
00:03:41.517 --> 00:03:45.841
Be careful! Don't say: I write three words for a two-word limit.

60
00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.461
Say: I copy no more than two words.

61
00:03:50.761 --> 00:03:52.087
Obey the limit.

62
00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:55.750
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:56.533 --> 00:03:58.092
Summary of a Study.

64
00:03:58.392 --> 00:04:01.657
A passage describes a study of sleep in teenagers.

65
00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:05.165
The summary has a gap that needs a noun phrase.

66
00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:09.118
The passage says teenagers need nine hours of rest.

67
00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:12.899
Students must write no more than two words for the gap.

68
00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:16.805
One student writes three words and loses the mark.

69
00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:21.925
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:22.783 --> 00:04:24.934
Before filling a gap, check blank.

71
00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:29.108
A, the word limit. B, the date. C, the page number.

72
00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:34.910
The answer is A: the word limit.

73
00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:37.887
Answers should come from blank.

74
00:04:38.187 --> 00:04:41.910
A, the dictionary. B, the passage. C, your memory.

75
00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:47.977
The answer is B: the passage.

76
00:04:49.117 --> 00:04:52.115
A summary often uses a blank for a passage word.

77
00:04:52.415 --> 00:04:55.685
A, number. B, map. C, synonym.

78
00:04:59.233 --> 00:05:01.384
The answer is C: synonym.

79
00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:03.981
Which should match the gap?

80
00:05:04.281 --> 00:05:08.561
A, grammar and meaning. B, only the spelling. C, only the length.

81
00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:15.144
The answer is A: grammar and meaning.

82
00:05:16.283 --> 00:05:18.051
What does the study describe?

83
00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:23.699
A, sport in school. B, sleep in teenagers. C, food in cities.

84
00:05:27.233 --> 00:05:30.440
The answer is B: sleep in teenagers.

85
00:05:31.633 --> 00:05:35.319
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:36.183 --> 00:05:38.253
How do you complete a summary correctly?

87
00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:48.620
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:48.920 --> 00:06:04.671
I read the instruction and the word limit first. I predict the type of word for each gap, then find the matching idea in the passage. I copy the exact word, and I read the sentence again to check the grammar and meaning.

89
00:06:04.971 --> 00:06:06.645
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:13.569
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: check meaning, grammar and word limit.

91
00:06:13.869 --> 00:06:18.762
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

92
00:06:19.062 --> 00:06:21.552
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

93
00:06:21.852 --> 00:06:24.969
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

